course: dictionary
lesson: 3679
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word flag is a good example. It can mean a piece of coloured cloth, a sign or signal, a way to mark something, or a way of saying you are getting tired.
explain: «Lifeguards move the flags during the day, because the safe place changes as the tide changes.» Here a flag is a sign that shows where it is safe to swim. The clues are safe and tide. Nobody is talking about cloth for a country.
explain: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» Here flag means the cloth itself, with its colours and stripes. Try the meaning in the sentence: a flag can have stripes, so it fits.
explain: «Its red breast is a warning flag» uses flag to mean a sign that warns others to keep away. To check any meaning, put it into the sentence. If it does not make sense, try another.
fact: Flag can be a noun (a flag, two flags) or a verb (to flag, he flags, he flagged, flagging).
fact: A flag is a piece of cloth with colours or pictures that stands for a country, a team or a group.
fact: A flag can also be a sign or signal, such as a red flag for danger or a chequered flag at the end of a race.
fact: As a verb, to flag something means to mark it so people notice it. To flag also means to get tired and slow down.
fact: Phrases to know: «wave a flag», «fly a flag», «red flag», and «flag down» (wave to stop a car).
exercise: «Lifeguards move the flags during the day, because the safe place changes as the tide changes.» What is a flag in this sentence? | A tired runner | Something you count in maths | *A sign that shows where it is safe to swim | A piece of cloth for a country's team
exercise: «The runner began to flag in the last mile.» What does flag mean here? | To mark something so people notice | *To get tired and slow down | To fly a country's flag | To wave a car to a stop
exercise: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» What colour is the top stripe? | Green | Red | *Blue | Yellow
test: Which meaning fits: to mark a mistake in your work so people notice it? | Count it | Wave it away | Fly it | *To flag it
test: «Its red breast is a warning flag.» What does flag mean here? | A tired bird | *A sign that warns others to keep away | A mark on a map of the garden | A piece of cloth for a country
exam: In «Please flag down the bus», what does flag down mean? | Count the buses | *Wave to make the bus stop | Sleep beside the bus | Paint the bus red
